      <p>Use the integration server to open menus, click buttons, enter text, and scroll panels from a script. You can automate the editor interface for screen recordings, end-to-end tests, and scripted demonstrations.</p>
      <p>To run DITA operations through an AI assistant, see <a href="/dogsbay-xml-docs/automation/mcp">Connecting an AI assistant</a>.</p>
      <h2 id="enabling-interface-automation" class="group scroll-mt-20">Enabling interface automation<a href="#enabling-interface-automation" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
      <p>Methods that run menu commands, enter text, or execute terminal commands require <code>--allow-driving</code>. The server token alone does not authorize these methods.</p>
      <Steps>
      <Step>
      <strong>Start the editor with interface automation enabled.</strong>
      <CodeBlock code={"dogsbay-xml gui --allow-driving"} lang="bash" />
